{"id": "EUVD-2026-86092", "enisaUuid": "0615a7f3-25d0-3474-b5ab-3599f9f8035f", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/amdgpu: validate and share PSP fw_pri_buf copies via psp_copy_fw\n\nChange psp_copy_fw from void to int: return -ENODEV when drm_dev_enter\nfails, and -EINVAL when the image size is zero or larger than the\n1 MiB PSP private buffer.\n\nReplace open-coded memset/memcpy into fw_pri_buf with psp_copy_fw.", "datePublished": "2026-09-24T16:04:41", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:52:55", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8ddda06ae356fda0418b7017e658d976dad6214e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/25bec2425c3d50ba9a92ad87bbf8628be29e5c32", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1aa55af304a2decaacca1d1fabe4257c277ca54a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d1f9f5839bd785a3a06335a01d53282e80f8e5fa"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-97494", "GHSA-gjv4-hxx3-7w8g"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "14303066-d302-30e1-b15d-e00f159e4f04", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.53"}, {"id": "3045f3c2-0f60-3b26-85db-c2a37b432dd1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "49a5508c-2dd6-3da7-b104-bdaf3cf05435", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2b0c3aee2172451e9f982b25f3fdf59a1b687dc3 <1aa55af304a2decaacca1d1fabe4257c277ca54a"}, {"id": "62f6adee-0933-3b38-a023-394d9d02b1e3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "69dd78b3-295e-3673-a204-31d884df635c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.12"}, {"id": "83edc2b5-91c8-347a-bd1d-525bc61853ca", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2b0c3aee2172451e9f982b25f3fdf59a1b687dc3 <25bec2425c3d50ba9a92ad87bbf8628be29e5c32"}, {"id": "9fd5e29